# Nidara's default terminal for "open in a terminal" (Terminal=true desktop entries,
# `uwsm app -T`), read by uwsm's terminal lookup (xdg-terminal-exec spec).
#
# A SYSTEM default, the lowest-priority place uwsm looks: a user's own
# ~/.config/xdg-terminals.list (or Hyprland-xdg-terminals.list) always wins.
# Without any list, uwsm picked org.gnome.Terminal.Preferences.desktop on a machine
# with GNOME Terminal installed — measured 2026-09-27.
#
# ⚠️ The desktop prefix is XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP verbatim: "Hyprland-", capital H.
# A "hyprland-xdg-terminals.list" is never read (measured).
kitty.desktop
